US-023 is verified and complete. The LOD and meshlet cooker was already in the tree from an earlier pass, so I checked it against the acceptance criteria and ran every gate. I changed no source code.

**What was already there**
- `cook_mesh()` in `tools/asset_converter/src/mesh_cooking.cpp` drops degenerate triangles and merges and reorders vertices. It builds up to 4 LODs at about half the triangles each. It splits each LOD into meshlets of at most 64 vertices and 124 triangles, and computes exact bounds.
- Small and degenerate meshes are handled: empty meshes cook to empty LODs, and a single triangle cooks to one LOD with one meshlet.
- meshoptimizer is built as `engine_meshopt_vendor`, which only the converter links. The runtime does not link it.
- The 11 cooking tests are in `tests/src/converter_mesh_tests.cpp`, and `docs/mesh-cooking.md` describes the design.

**What this pass fixed**
- The earlier run said US-023 passed, but `tasks/prd.json` still had `passes: false` and `.ralph-tui/progress.md` had no US-023 entry. I set the flag and appended the entry.
